        "original_id": "fd8d79e3-9717-534a-870d-67bdcb42e2b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tahmoh Penikett, Joss Whedon\n- Characters: Karl C. Agathon\n- Organizations: Mutant Enemy Productions, Bellwether Pictures\n- Television series: Supernatural, Dollhouse, Continuum, Buffy the Vampire Slayer, Angel, Firefly, Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D., Battlestar Galactica\n\nFacts:\n- Joss Whedon founded Mutant Enemy Productions and co-founded Bellwether Pictures.\n- From 1997 to 2003, Joss Whedon created the television series Buffy the Vampire Slayer.\n- From 1999 to 2004, Joss Whedon created the television series Angel.\n- In 2002, Joss Whedon created the television series Firefly.\n- From 2009 to 2010, Joss Whedon created the television series Dollhouse.\n- Tahmoh Penikett starred in the television series Supernatural, Dollhouse, and Continuum.\n- In the re-imagined Battlestar Galactica television series, Karl C. Agathon, also called Helo, is a fictional character portrayed by Tahmoh Penikett.\n- From 2013, Joss Whedon created the television series Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1ab2db32-be08-5663-804e-1718f41691ed",
        "text": "Page: Tahmoh Penikett. Sentence: He has starred in TV series \"Supernatural\", Joss Whedon's \"Dollhouse\", and the Showtime time travel show, \"Continuum\".\nPage: Joss Whedon. Sentence: He is the founder of Mutant Enemy Productions and co-founder of Bellwether Pictures, and is best known as the creator of the television series \"Buffy the Vampire Slayer\" (1997–2003), \"Angel\" (1999–2004), \"Firefly\" (2002), \"Dollhouse\" (2009–10) and \"Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.\" (from 2013).\nPage: Karl Agathon. Sentence: Karl C. Agathon (callsign \"Helo\") is a fictional character on the re-imagined \"Battlestar Galactica\" TV series, portrayed by Tahmoh Penikett.",
